{"t": 1792645617202, "cmd": "note", "args": ["--shot", "sell_ambiguous", "Clicked 'Sell Resources' in my own settlement right after building its only stall (tick ~8120), carrying 30 apples/10 wood/5 stone. Status: 'No one is buying resources at this market or you do not have enough resources to sell.' Root cause (Market.sellResources) is that you cannot sell to your own stall, and the other merchant listed (Abigail Thompson) has no stall/coins; the message hides this. Expected: 'You can't sell to your own stall - sell at another settlement's market' (or show which stalls can pay). Market Info also shows 'Merchants: Abigail Thompson' which suggests she would buy."]}
