{"t": 1792645812840, "cmd": "note", "args": ["--shot", "sold1", "Selling at Whiteburg (ticks 11287-11851): each 'Sell Resources' click sold ONE unit (1 stone +16, 1 stone +9, 1 wood +26), and the status only says 'You sold resources to Abigail Davies. Relationship increased to 2.' - never what was sold or for how much; I had to diff my inventory. After 3 sales the market (45 coins total) was dry and 31 apples / 14 saplings never sold at all, with the same ambiguous 'No one is buying...' message. Trade feels like click-grinding for tiny sums; expected a quantity choice and a sale receipt ('Sold 1 stone for 16 coins')."]}
